From 1cd1ecc706b58e2472cc91b71e3f6a8c93fe263f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:17:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] loop_accounting: per-pass CPU accounting for Kanban
 loops and polled routes (P1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Card A (t_01a1d59c4cdf97ba) of design t_01a1d563324d7e8e §2 P1 / C17, with review R3.

New hermes_cli/loop_accounting.py: per pass name, runs / skips / key changes /
fallbacks / rows / errors and time.thread_time() CPU (sum, max) plus wall time;
per thread, /proc/self/task CPU next to the CPU its outermost passes accounted
(R3), so the hub's unattributed CPU lands on a thread. Gateway, serve and tui
processes (shared_metrics_process.begin_process) write an atomic JSON snapshot
every 60 s to <root>/run/loop-accounting/<pid>.json (config.yaml
loop_accounting.enabled / interval_s). API: pass_(name, skipped=, changed=,
fallback=, rows=), timed(), @accounted(name, rows=), span_open/span_close.

Wired: sync.board/<slug> (sync_timing board hooks), dispatcher.tick,
dispatcher.board/<slug>, dispatch.<sweep> for every dispatch_once sub-sweep,
dispatcher.auto_decompose, notifier.collect(+_board/<slug>),
unloaded.host_pass and its sub-passes, unloaded.residual_pass,
remote_index.refresh/compute, links_refresh, machine_metrics.tick,
change_watcher.pass and change_watcher/<event>, notifications.<poll>,
annotation.refresh/poll/revalidate/holder_refresh/<profile>, rpc/<method>,
producer_admission.sweep, route/profiles.sessions(.sidebar),
route/profiles.projects.tree, route/kanban.board, route/sessions.kanban_tasks.
HostLoopLease records lease.<name> from a true held() to its beat(), so mod host
passes (chat-closeout _host_pass) are accounted with no mod change.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_loop_accounting.py (counters, nesting, spans,
lease, overflow, per-thread CPU, snapshot file, writer, prune, begin_process,
sync hooks, exited-thread folding without procfs); test_loop_accounting_bench.py
pins <= 20 us per pass.

Exited threads fold into exited_accounted at each snapshot. Without procfs
(macOS Desktop/serve/TUI backends, whose native thread ids are never reused)
the live set comes from threading.enumerate(), so short-lived worker threads
cannot grow the per-thread map.

Boundary lint: the kanban dashboard (plugins/kanban/dashboard/plugin_api.py)
already imports hermes_cli.kanban_* internals; its one new
hermes_cli.loop_accounting import (route/kanban.board accounting) is
intended and recorded in scripts/boundary_lint_baseline.json.
